WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.775
Here’s something that surprises people.

2
00:00:03.025 --> 00:00:07.150
Most wrong answers in this lesson aren’t navigation mistakes.

3
00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:09.250
They’re clock mistakes.

4
00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:11.900
Use the twenty-four hour clock.

5
00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:15.575
One thirty in the afternoon is thirteen thirty.

6
00:00:15.825 --> 00:00:19.525
When you add minutes, carry at sixty, not at one hundred.

7
00:00:19.775 --> 00:00:22.425
Nine forty-five plus fifty minutes.

8
00:00:22.675 --> 00:00:24.150
What is it?

9
00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:26.950
Ten thirty-five.

10
00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:30.500
Not nine ninety-five, and not ten ninety-five.

11
00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:33.450
Decimal hours are another trap.

12
00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:38.625
One point seven five hours is not one hour seventy-five minutes.

13
00:00:38.875 --> 00:00:41.925
Multiply the decimal part by sixty.

14
00:00:42.175 --> 00:00:44.850
It’s one hour and forty-five minutes.

15
00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:50.450
Going the other way, one hundred five minutes is one hour and forty-five minutes.

16
00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:56.300
And on a trip with several legs, work out each leg’s time by itself, then add them up.
